  - reward-shaping
  - tile-coding
abstract: >-
  A reproducible empirical study of on-policy SARSA(lambda) with tile coding,
  DQN with and without experience replay, potential-based reward shaping, and a
  controlled rapid-exploration-decay intervention on Gymnasium MountainCar-v0.
  Five training seeds, 20 held-out evaluation episodes per seed, and a locked
  60,000-interaction budget per learned run. The strongest measured condition
  was tile-coded SARSA(lambda): 1.000 completion within 200 steps and 0.380
  assignment-success within 100 steps; no condition reliably met the 100-step
  target.
